      "extract": "In a talk at the Mittag-Leﬄer Institute in May 1999, K. Habiro announced a new approach to computing the colored Jones polynomial of knots and quantum sl2 invariants of integral homology 3-spheres. For an exposition, see his paper [H2] (some results are already announced in [H1]). His invariant for homology spheres recovers both the sl2 Reshetikhin-Turaev invariants at roots of unity, and Ohtsuki’s power series",
      "extractCut": true
