      "extract": "Graphical calculus and a formula for ωp Let us write ω = ω+ and put ωp = ∞ X n=0 cn,pRn . (23) Note that the coeﬃcients cn,p are well-deﬁned (because Rn divides Rn+1 and therefore the coeﬃcients Ck n,m in the product expansion RnRm = P k Ck n,mRk are zero if n or m is bigger than k.) We have ⟨ωp, x⟩= ⟨tp(x)⟩ (24) for every even x. (This follows from (6) since circling with ωp is the same as circling with p parallel",
