      "extract": "Another formula for the coeﬃcients of ωp Following Habiro, we introduce the polynomials R′ n = ({n}!)−1Rn and write ωp = ∞ X n=0 c′ n,pR′ n , (34) where c′ n,p = {n}! cn,p . The aim of this section is to show that c′ n,p is a Laurent polynomial, i.e. that c′ n,p ∈Z[A±]. This fact was shown by Habiro [H3] using the quantum group Uqsl2. Observe that by (9) and (7), we already know this fact for p = ±1: c′ n,1 =",
